  "solveSteps": [
    "$s = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}x}{x-1}$을 $x$에 대하여 풀면 $x = \\dfrac{s}{s-\\sqrt{3}}$이므로 $x_A = \\dfrac{t}{t-\\sqrt{3}}$, $x_B = \\dfrac{3}{3-\\sqrt{3}}$이다.",
    "$\\overline{AH} = t-3$이고, $\\overline{BH} = x_B - x_A = \\dfrac{3(t-\\sqrt{3})-t(3-\\sqrt{3})}{(3-\\sqrt{3})(t-\\sqrt{3})} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}(t-3)}{(3-\\sqrt{3})(t-\\sqrt{3})}$이므로\n\n$$\\lim_{t\\to 3+}\\frac{\\overline{AH}}{\\overline{BH}} = \\lim_{t\\to 3+}\\frac{(3-\\sqrt{3})(t-\\sqrt{3})}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{(3-\\sqrt{3})^2}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{12-6\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} = 4\\sqrt{3} - 6$$\n\n따라서 $a=-6,\\ b=4$이므로 $a+b = -2$이다.",
    "정답은 ①이다."
  ],
